{"id": "EUVD-2026-97434", "enisaUuid": "3e60e7bf-be53-383f-b964-566cf9c1c140", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.21 contains a resource budget bypass vulnerability that allows remote attackers to override GLM-V video processing limits by supplying fps, max_frames, max_tokens_per_frame and max_image_tokens in the video_url object. Attackers can set these values arbitrarily high so glm4v.py decodes every frame of high-resolution video at full size, exhausting worker memory and denying service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T14:04:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:52:09", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43705", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/openai/protocol.py#L592-L594", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/parser/conversation.py#L691", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/multimodal/processors/glm4v.py#L160-L167", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/multimodal/processors/glm4v.py#L400", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.21-resource-budget-bypass-via-glm-v-video-parameters"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2mhj-6r3c-c9xj", "CVE-2026-109228"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4c9223bb-8630-31e7-a133-ac773f1a1cbc", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.21"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "768da30c-55d9-35ff-8d4a-3da4ec28d31c", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}